<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The Miscalculated Element</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Adora Grey is one of the most skilled &lt;i&gt;Federated Territories&lt;/i&gt; agents, often assigned with special deployments of the government. She goes where the Federation needs her. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catra Driluth is the best &lt;i&gt;Horde&lt;/i&gt; operative they have, tasked with the most delicate solo missions of her mob. And she loves nothing more than to play her most hated enemy out. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It hasnâ€™t always been so, but times need hard decisions, and in Adoraâ€™s eyes, Catra made the wrong one when she betrayed her, back then. Today, when they clash, they spare each other nothing.&lt;br /&gt;Colliding again at the Grand Opera over Fhloston Paradise will set in a series of events, that will leave their worlds and beliefs in shatters. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Because they miscalculated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;____________________________&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;Catradora&lt;/i&gt; in the world of the Fifth Element, in the middle of all the havoc that happened at the cruise ship and that we just didn't get to see on-screen in the actual movie from 1997 because of - obviously - budget-reasons? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don't worry, I have you. This crossover will be nothing but pure chaos, &lt;b&gt;Wuhuuu!!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>21st_tikonda</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Teen And Up Audiences</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Fifth Element (1997)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora/Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Crossover</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>F/F</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Angella (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Jean-Baptiste Emanuel Zorg</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Snarky Adora</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Snarky Catra</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>They need to talk a lot</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Leeloo (Fifth Element)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>This is all chaos just like in the movie</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>I had so much fun putting this down</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Is Adora Bruce Willis' secret sister?</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra is a tease but how could she not in the sight of the blonde idiot</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Angella in a uniform looks hot</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>mean language</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Many fucks are given</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>This isn't an AU but a side string of the movie plot</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>They rather hit the shit out of each other than talk</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Rapid viewpoint switches</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Korben Dallas</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Mangalores</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>A boob window as a strategic mean</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>i wrote this for me but you can read it if you want</rdf:li>
